Manual Testing 

Principles:
Testing shows the presence of defects(Tests will simply show if you are on the good path to achieving the expected results)
Exhaustive Testing is not possible(it is not practical to test every possible scenario, path, and input combination)
Early Testing(good)
Defect Clustering (most of the bugs are coming from other bugs or have the same root cause)
Pesticide Paradox (testing is same way not generate new bugs)
Testing is context-dependent(Not all testing approaches work in each project.)
Absence of errors fallacy(identify your client's needs incorrectly)

